    "behavioral-questions": { notes: ["Use STAR as a guide: Situation, Task, Action, Result. Spend most of the answer on your actions and learning.", "Choose a specific event, describe your own decisions, and report an honest result without exaggerating.", "For conflict or failure questions, explain how you responded and what you changed afterward."], questions: makeQuestions("behavioral-questions", [["Easy", "In STAR, what does the R represent?", ["Result", "Review", "Risk", "Role"], 0, "STAR stands for Situation, Task, Action, Result."], ["Medium", "A behavioral answer is strongest when it:", ["Uses a specific example and clarifies your actions", "Stays entirely hypothetical", "Avoids the outcome", "Blames teammates"], 0, "Specific evidence and personal ownership make the example credible and useful."], ["Medium", "When discussing a failure, include:", ["What you learned and changed afterward", "Only who was at fault", "An invented success", "No context"], 0, "Reflection demonstrates learning and how behavior changed after the event."]]) },
